NT_CODE) per year).\n\n**6b. SQL approach:** Three per-year aggregations (different filter scopes per the question wording), joined on ACADEMIC_YEAR:\n1. variance CTE: TIP_DETAIL ⋈ ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL ⋈ ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER on TERM_CODE, term-parameter filter, `VARIANCE(RECORD_COUNT)`.\n2. geometric-mean CTE: TIP_DETAIL ⋈ ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL on TERM_CODE, `TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY='RQ' AND RECORD_COUNT>0`, `EXP(AVG(LN(RECORD_COUNT)))`.\n3. department CTE: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED ⋈ ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL on TERM_CODE, `COUNT(DISTINCT DEPARTMENT_CODE)`.\nInner-join on ACADEMIC_YEAR (precedent dw_4701), select exactly the 5 requested columns in order, ORDER BY variance DESC, no ROUND anywhere. Caveats: no direct TIP_DETAIL↔catalog join exists in the hinted join keys, so no td×ccso fan-out is introduced; VARIANCE() is MySQL's population variance, matching precedents dw_2958/dw_41.\n\n**6c. Three-perspective reasons:**\n- **Data**: RECORD_COUNT and TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY physically exist on TIP_DETAIL (column defs retrieved); TERM_CODE exists on all four tables (column_concept_term_code); ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER holds exactly 3 rows so the IN-filter is safe and cannot fan out; grouping CTEs by (ACADEMIC_YEAR, ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC) keeps one row per year since the description is a year attribute (precedent dw_2957 groups identically).\n- **Semantic network**: concept_academic_term_dimension decision_guide mandates ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER for \"current/previous term\" references and ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL for academic-year attributes; column_concept_material_status_key decision_guide mandates 'RQ' for \"required\"; hint join keys are exactly the three TERM_CODE joins used.\n- **Business**: dw_4701/dw_3417 establish the per-measure-scope CTE pattern for same-shape \"For each academic year, what is …\" questions; dw_2957/dw_4061 establish EXP(AVG(LN())) with a >0 guard; dw_2958/dw_41 establish bare VARIANCE() and variance-descending ordering.\n\n**6d. Alternatives/tie-breaker:** A single-query variant (all filters in one WHERE, td×ccso joined through the term) was considered and rejected: it would apply the RQ/>0 filter to the variance and the term-parameter filter to the department count, contradicting the question's per-measure filter attachment, and it creates a term-level cross-product fan-out with no hinted join key. The tie-breaker fact would have been the gold's execution plan/data sizes, but the database was unreachable (auth error on every attempt).\n\nFinal SQL:\n\n",
      "tool_calls": [
